# The verification programs that cannot pass on Linux (OpenSpec change m7-linux, design D6): <name><TAB><reason>, as
# known.list. A reason that starts with "windows" skips the program there; any other makes its failure known. Read
# by tools/legacy_tests/run_legacy_tests.py --platform linux. Each line was measured with QB64pe's Linux build too.
v22_d_shell	windows: SHELLs cmd; on Linux the shell's "not found" comes between the program's lines in another order each run
v29_a_sound_queue	varies: ALSA's null device plays nothing, so the queue's length changes from run to run; crashes now and then (munmap_chunk)
v29_d_volume_zero	varies: ALSA's null device plays nothing, so the queue's length changes from run to run
v29_f_queue_slice	varies: ALSA's null device plays nothing, so the queue's length changes from run to run; QB64pe's build crashed recording it
v29_g_voice	varies: ALSA's null device plays nothing, so the voices' lengths change from run to run
v39_c_files_raw_midi	varies: a raw sound on ALSA's null device crashes now and then, in QB64pe's build too (as corpus slice/s129)
v40_a_all_keys	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_b_numeric_only	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_c_order	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
v40_d_forms	windows: reads the executable's version information with PowerShell
